470 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 126 0 R/E(Let\220s start with Cronus, a Titan who rose to power by overthrowing his father. He was warned that one of his children would overthrow him. Determined to avoid this fate, Cronus began devouring his newborns, one by one.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

471 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 126 0 R/E(But prophecy doesn\220t fear cruelty. Rhea, his wife, tricked him with a swaddled stone and hid the real baby, Zeus, who grew up in secret, returned in power, and fulfilled the prophecy. Years later, Zeus forced Cronus to vomit up his siblings and dethroned him. Not only did Zeus overthrow Cronus, but he also established a new order of gods atop Mount Olympus.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

